```

This allows you to import existing keys into your Terraform state, enabling management of keys that were created outside of Terraform.

litellm:index/keyBlock:KeyBlock.description:
## #<span pulumi-lang-nodejs=" litellm.KeyBlock " pulumi-lang-dotnet=" litellm.KeyBlock " pulumi-lang-go=" KeyBlock " pulumi-lang-python=" KeyBlock " pulumi-lang-yaml=" litellm.KeyBlock " pulumi-lang-java=" litellm.KeyBlock " pulumi-lang-hcl=" litellm_key_block "> litellm.KeyBlock </span>Resource

Manages the blocked state of an existing LiteLLM API key. Creating this resource blocks the key; destroying it unblocks the key.

If the key is unblocked outside of Terraform (or deleted), the resource is removed from state and Terraform plans to re-block it on the next apply.

