* JSON strings (starting with `[` or `{`) are parsed as JSON objects/arrays
* Non-convertible strings remain strings
* The provider merges these keys into the <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`litellmParams`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`LitellmParams`" pulumi-lang-go="`litellmParams`" pulumi-lang-python="`litellm_params`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`litellmParams`" pulumi-lang-java="`litellmParams`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`litellm_params`">`litellmParams`</span> payload sent to the API.
* Note: the remote API may not echo back all custom parameters; this provider preserves <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`additionalLitellmParams`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`AdditionalLitellmParams`" pulumi-lang-go="`additionalLitellmParams`" pulumi-lang-python="`additional_litellm_params`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`additionalLitellmParams`" pulumi-lang-java="`additionalLitellmParams`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`additional_litellm_params`">`additionalLitellmParams`</span> in state when present in configuration.

